  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{CaCl}_{2}$ is produced as a byproduct in solvay ammonia process.\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\text { (i) } \\mathrm{NaCl}+\\mathrm{CO}_{2}+\\mathrm{NH}_{3}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\longrightarrow \\mathrm{NaHCO}_{3}+\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n(I) $\\mathrm{CaCO}_{3} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{CO}_{2}+\\mathrm{CaO}$\r\n\r\n $2 \\mathrm{NH}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}+\\mathrm{CaO} \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{NH}_{3}+$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\mathrm{CaCl}_{2}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{C}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nBy podust",
